    dict(key='01-poster', kind='poster', title='Cross-Site Scripting with Spring Boot',
         body=None,
         narration="Hello, and welcome. [[slnc 400]] This video looks at cross site scripting defences in Spring Boot. [[slnc 300]] This video is presented by Jayasekhar Konduru. [[slnc 600]] First, a reminder. [[slnc 300]] Cross site scripting happens when a customer's text is read by the browser as part of the page. [[slnc 300]] The defence is to encode every value for the place it is written. [[slnc 600]] Think of a shop that prints customers' reviews through a printer that always prints plain letters. [[slnc 300]] The printer has one switch that prints a note as the shop's own sign. [[slnc 300]] Flip it for a customer's note, and the note passes as the shop. [[slnc 700]] In this video, the domain is an online store. [[slnc 500]] By the end, you will hear what Thymeleaf escapes for you. [[slnc 300]] The one switch that stops it. [[slnc 300]] How each place a value goes is escaped. [[slnc 300]] And how to send a policy with a fresh nonce from Spring Security."),
